1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:18,504
An open-shelf built-in bookcase for Dan Lee’s home office: three 32" tall units filling a 96" wall, no doors.

2
00:00:18,504 --> 00:00:25,805
Start from the Tall 24" x 84" pantry preset: it already has the tall carcass and shelf-pin rows a bookcase needs.

3
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:43,704
Open it. Width 32": 96" divided by three. Depth 12": books don’t need a 24" pantry.

4
00:00:43,704 --> 00:00:50,786
Doors: None. An open unit has no doors, hinges or boring, and its shelves become the face of the piece.

5
00:00:50,786 --> 00:00:58,149
Why 32" wide? A 3/4" shelf over ~30" spans fine for books. Wider units want a thicker shelf or a centre support, or the shelves sag.

6
00:00:58,149 --> 00:01:03,598
Shelves: 5 adjustable. Six openings of about 13", tall enough for most books and binders.

7
00:01:03,598 --> 00:01:12,353
Shelf-pin rows: 5 mm holes on a 32 mm pitch, front and back. 32 mm is the system spacing every line-boring head and pin uses.

8
00:01:12,353 --> 00:01:20,170
The front row is set back from the front edge so the pin holes don’t show and the edge doesn’t break out.

9
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:27,109
Banding matters more on open shelves: the shelf front is what you see. Use the 1 mm ABS, not the 0.4 mm tape that suits hidden edges.

10
00:01:27,109 --> 00:01:32,861
Carcass front edges get 1 mm too: the sides and top of an open unit are on show as well.

11
00:01:32,861 --> 00:01:43,468
The parts table: two sides, top, bottom, back and five shelves, each with the edges it bands.

12
00:01:43,468 --> 00:01:50,040
Copy it twice: the three units are identical, so set one up and duplicate it.

13
00:01:50,040 --> 00:02:05,297
The room: a 96" wall. Arrange puts the three units side by side, wall to wall.

14
00:02:05,297 --> 00:02:13,921
Elevation: no doors, so you see every shelf. Check the openings line up across the three units: same shelf count, same heights.

15
00:02:13,921 --> 00:02:27,025
In 3D: one built-in run, 96" x 84" x 12".

16
00:02:27,025 --> 00:02:37,424
Cut list: 15 shelves, all the same size, each banded on its front edge with the 1 mm ABS.

17
00:02:37,424 --> 00:02:43,681
Hardware: no hinges or slides. Shelf pins, four per shelf (60), and the Confirmat screws that join the carcass.

18
00:02:43,681 --> 00:02:50,645
Nesting: 12" deep parts nest tightly, so three tall units fit on few sheets.

19
00:02:50,645 --> 00:02:58,385
The labels show the pin holes on each side: the drilling the machine does, so the shelves go in level.

20
00:02:58,385 --> 00:03:04,829
So: open units come from a tall preset: set width for shelf span, depth for the contents, doors None, and show-face banding.
